 --> 00:00:50.519\narchitectural motifs, ancient designs\n\ncue-20\n00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.539\nreinterpreted today in broccatello.\n\ncue-21\n00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:56.439\nSilk, cotton, and linen give volume to\n\ncue-22\n00:00:56.439 --> 00:00:58.999\nthe surface. The light changes. The\n\ncue-23\n00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.939\ntextile comes to life, and tradition\n\ncue-24\n00:01:01.939 --> 00:01:03.059\ncontinues to live on.\n",lw="WEBVTT\n\ncue-1\n00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:00.799\nAscolta.\n\ncue-2\n00:00:01.519 --> 00:00:03.719\nIl fruscio della stoffa non è solo\n\ncue-3\n00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.000\nsuono, è ritmo, è metodo, è memoria.\n\ncue-4\n00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:09.939\nSiamo a Firenze, alla Fondazione Arte\n\ncue-5\n00:00:09.939 --> 00:00:13.779\ndella Seta Lisio. Qui dal 1906 i disegni\n\ncue-6\n00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:15.960\nnon restano negli archivi, tornano a\n\ncue-7\n00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.180\nvivere nei tessuti. Tutto comincia con\n\ncue-8\n00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.579\nuna messa in carta, un disegno tecnico\n\ncue-9\n00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:22.839\nsu carta millimetrata. Da lì nascono i\n\ncue-10\n00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.739\ncartoni jacquard che traducono il\n\ncue-11\n00:00:24.739 --> 00:00:27.239\ndisegno in istruzioni tecniche. È un\n\ncue-12\n00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:29.739\nprocesso preciso, fatto di prove,\n\ncue-13\n00:00:29.739 --> 00:00:32.119\ncorrezioni e campionature fino a\n\ncue-14\n00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:34.439\nraggiungere il risultato finale. Per la\n\ncue-15\n00:00:34.439 --> 00:00:36.759\nPasticcino Bag World Tour - Italian\n\ncue-16\n00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:39.419\nRoots, Weekend Max Mara ha esplorato\n\ncue-17\n00:00:39.419 --> 00:00:41.500\nquesto archivio di pattern storici,\n\ncue-18\n00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.680\ngeometrie rinascimentali, motivi\n\ncue-19\n00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.000\narchitettonici, disegni antichi\n\ncue-20\n00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.739\nreinterpretati oggi in broccatello.\n\ncue-21\n00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:50.599\nSeta, cotone e lino danno\n\ncue-22\n00:00:50.599 --> 00:00:53.459\n volume alla superficie. La luce cambia,\n\ncue-23\n00:00:53.459 --> 00:00:56.359\nla materia prende forma e la tradizione\n\ncue-24\n00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.159\ncontinua a vivere.\n",cw="/static/voice-chapter-02-en-BXs2cnXh.mp3",uw="/static/voice-chapter-02-it-BGPsBdvi.mp3",dw="WEBVTT\n\ncue-1\n00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:02.439\nEach place on this journey tells the\n\ncue-2\n00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.279\nstory of a different material.\n\ncue-3\n00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:07.679\nIn Florence, we encountered fabric.\n\ncue-4\n00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:10.519\nHere we encounter stone.\n\ncue-5\n00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:13.899\nFor the Pasticcino Bag World Tour - \n\ncue-6\n00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:17.579\nItalian Roots project, Weekend Max Mara\n\ncue-7\n00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:20.099\nintroduces into the collection one of\n\ncue-8\n00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.699\nthe most iconic materials of Italian\n\ncue-9\n00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:23.260\nculture:\n\ncue-10\n00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:24.719\nmarble.\n\ncue-11\n00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:30.059\nBianco Carrara, Bardiglio, Verde Alpi,\n\ncue-12\n00:00:30.059 --> 00:00:31.119\nFior di Pesco,\n\ncue-13\n00:00:31.739 --> 00:00:35.299\nthe precious Nero Portoro, Calacatta,\n\ncue-14\n00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:36.200\nblack marble.\n\ncue-15\n00:00:37.139 --> 00:00:39.539\nStones that for centuries have shaped\n\ncue-16\n00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.539\nbasilicas, piazzas, and sculptures.\n\ncue-17\n00:00:43.659 --> 00:00:46.199\nFrom a marble slab, small blocks of\n\ncue-18\n00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.159\nstone are cut.\n\ncue-19\n00:00:47.759 --> 00:00:51.000\nThey are shaped, worked, polished.\n\ncue-20\n00:00:51.959 --> 00:00:54.439\nLittle by little, the surface changes.\n\ncue-21\n00:00:55.159 --> 00:00:57.379\nThe veining emerges, the color,\n\ncue-22\n00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.599\nthe depth of the material.\n\ncue-23\n00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:02.520\nStone finds a new scale,\n\ncue-24\n00:01:03.299 --> 00:01:05.879\nno longer monumental architecture, but a\n\ncue-25\n00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:07.159\nprecious detail.\n\ncue-26\n00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:11.159\nA small marble sphere that defines the\n\ncue-27\n00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:12.519\nPasticcino bag\n",hw="WEBVTT\n\ncue-1\n00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.939\nOgni luogo di questo viaggio racconta\n\ncue-2\n00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:02.919\nuna materia diversa.\n\ncue-3\n00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:05.920\nA Firenze abbiamo incontrato il tessuto.\n\ncue-4\n00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.899\nQui incontriamo la pietra.\n\ncue-5\n00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.219\nPer il progetto Pasticcino Bag World\n\ncue-6\n00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:12.420\nTour - Italian Roots,\n\ncue-7\n00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:14.739\nWeekend Max Mara introduce nella\n\ncue-8\n00:00:14.739 --> 00:00:17.000\ncollezione uno dei materiali più iconici\n\ncue-9\n00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.139\ndella cultura italiana: il marmo.\n\ncue-10\n00:00:19.959 --> 00:00:22.479\nBianco Carrara, Bardiglio, Verde Alpi,\n\ncue-11\n00:00:22.479 --> 00:00:25.119\nFior di Pesco, il prezioso Nero Portoro,\n\ncue-12\n00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.819\nCalacatta, Marmo Nero.\n\ncue-13\n00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:29.279\nPietre che da secoli attraversano\n\ncue-14\n00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.059\nbasiliche, piazze e sculture.\n\ncue-15\n00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:33.779\nDa una lastra di marmo nascono piccoli\n\ncue-16\n00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:36.299\nblocchi di pietra, vengono tagliati,\n\ncue-17\n00:00:36.299 --> 00:00:37.719\nlavorati, lucidati.\n\ncue-18\n00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:40.680\nPoco alla volta la superficie cambia,\n\ncue-19\n00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.020\nemergono le venature, il colore, la\n\ncue-20\n00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.239\nprofondità del materiale.\n\ncue-21\n00:00:44.939 --> 00:00:46.500\nLa pietra trova una nuova scala.\n\ncue-22\n00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:49.279\nNon più architettura monumentale, ma un\n\ncue-23\n00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:50.500\ndettaglio prezioso,\n\ncue-24\n00:00:51.119 --> 00:00:53.399\nuna piccola perla di marmo che definisce\n\ncue-25\n00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:54.520\nla Pasticcino Bag\n",fw=.1,pw={Chapter01:{key:"chapter01",locales:{en:{src:rw,subtitles:Bd(ow)},it:{src:aw,subtitles:Bd(lw)}}},Chapter02:{key:"chapter02",locales:{en:{src:cw,subtitles:Bd(dw)},it:{src:uw,subtitles:Bd(hw)}}}},Ji=jn(null),Yg=jn(null),Kg=jn(null),Ya=jn(""),hr=jn(!1),Nc=jn(0),bf=jn(0);Et(()=>Nc.value>0||hr.value);const Xu=new Map;let Ua=-1,hs=null;const{resume:mw,pause:Gh}=dE(()=>{const r=Cf();if(!r)return;const e=r.howl.seek();if(typeof e!="number")return;const t=bf.value||r.howl.duration()||0;t>0&&(Nc.value=Math.min(1,e/t)),vw(r.subtitles,e)},{immediate:!1});function gw(r,e="en"){var s;const t=r?pw[r]:void 0;if(!r||!t){Q_();return}const n=yE(e,t),i=vE(t.key,n);Ji.value!==i&&Q_(),yw(r,e,t),Ji.value=i,Yg.value=r,Kg.value=n,bf.value=((s=Xu.get(i))==null?void 0:s.howl.duration())||0,setTimeout(jg,1e3)}function jg(){const r=Cf();if(!(!r||Ql.value)){if(r.howl.volume(r.volume),hs!==null){if(r.howl.playing(hs))return;r.howl.play(hs);return}hs=r.howl.play()}}function Aw(){const r=Cf();r&&(hs===null?r.howl.pause():r.howl.pause(hs))}function _w(){hr.value?Aw():jg()}function xw(){const r=Cf();r&&(hs===null?r.howl.seek(0):r.howl.seek(0,hs),Ua=-1,Ya.value="",Nc.value=0,jg())}function Q_(){Xu.forEach(r=>{r.howl.stop(),r.howl.volume(r.volume)}),Sw()}function yw(r,e,t){var c,u;const n=yE(e,t),i=t.locales[n],s=vE(t.key,n),a=Xu.get(s);if((a==null?void 0:a.src)===i.src)return;a==null||a.howl.unload();const o=(c=t.volume)!=null?c:fw,l=new sI.Howl({src:[i.src],preload:!0,volume:o});l.on("load",()=>{Ji.value===s&&(bf.value=l.duration())}),l.on("play",d=>{Ji.value===s&&(hs=d,hr.value=!0,mw())}),l.on("pause",()=>{Ji.value===s&&(hr.value=!1,Gh())}),l.on("stop",()=>{Ji.value===s&&(hs=null,hr.value=!1,Nc.value=0,Ya.value="",Ua=-1,Gh())}),l.on("end",()=>{Ji.value===s&&(hs=null,hr.value=!1,Ya.value="",Ua=-1,Gh())}),Xu.set(s,{howl: